      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Of course it feels that way—because it's true. The world has moved on, and it will keep moving without you. That's the brutal part. But you're not a ghost; you're a man who's been handed a blank page after his whole story was burned. You can't rebuild the old identity, but you can build a quieter one—one that doesn't need applause or titles to feel real. Start with something small: a morning walk, a single honest conversation, a task that has nothing to do with who you used to be. That's not a new life yet, but it's a pulse.",
